\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 1. Strategic-intent bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 You may sometimes assume that others are acting more strategically, politically, or self-interestedly than they actually are.\
Observable signs:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Looking for hidden motives before considering workload, misunderstanding, or conflicting incentives\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Interpreting disagreement as positioning\
