\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\fs42 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Direct\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I\'92m working on how I make decisions under pressure. In that discussion, was there anything I did that made it harder to disagree with me?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Behaviour-specific\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I\'92m trying to separate decisive leadership from closing discussion too quickly. Did I invite enough challenge before making the call?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Lower-pressure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93You do not need to answer immediately. If you notice me attributing motives, interrupting dissent, or becoming overly sharp under pressure, I would value a private signal.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I want to respond thoughtfully rather than quickly. Unless there is an immediate operational risk, I\'92m going to review the facts and come back by tomorrow.\'94\
\'93I notice that I\'92m frustrated, so I do not want to make a consequential decision in that state. Let\'92s pause and return to the issue at a defined time.\'94\
\'93Before we act, I want to separate what we know from what we are inferring.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93The core idea came from [name], and [name] provided the evidence that made it workable. My role was to help bring the decision together.\'94\
\'93I want the record to reflect that this outcome depended substantially on [specific contribution].\'94\
\'93I built on work that was already underway. The original insight and much of the implementation belong to the team.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93My wording in that meeting was sharper than it needed to be, and addressing it publicly may have made the situation worse. I\'92m sorry. I should have raised the concern privately and focused on the specific work issue.\'94\
\'93I intended to move the work forward, but the impact was that you did not have a fair opportunity to respond. I take responsibility for that. I will reopen the relevant part of the process and make the criteria explicit.\'94\
\'93I realise I treated my interpretation of your motives as fact. That was not fair. I should have asked you directly. Is there anything factual I need to correct with others?\'94\
A repair should not pressure the other person to forgive, reassure you, or disclose more than they wish.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93Let\'92s distinguish the substantive disagreement, the process concern, and the interpersonal impact. We may need different responses to each.\'94\
\'93I disagree with your conclusion, but I want to represent your reasoning accurately. Let me summarise what I think you are saying.\'94\
\'93We should use the same standard we would apply if the roles were reversed.\'94\
\'93I will not make assumptions about intent. Let\'92s focus first on the observable behaviour, its impact, and what needs to change.\'94\
\'93Because there is a power difference here, I want to make sure you have a safe route to raise concerns, including through someone other than me.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa375\partightenfactor0

