\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 7. Final caution\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 These results should be interpreted 
\f1\b cautiously and non-diagnostically
\f0\b0 . Scores on traits labelled narcissism, Machiavellianism, psychopathy, or sadism do not establish a personality disorder, predict a particular act, or define your moral character. Without the instrument\'92s manual, norms, psychometric quality, response-validity information, and assessment context, precise claims would be unwarranted. Psychological assessment guidance emphasises appropriate interpretation, multiple sources of information, and attention to context and limitations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apa.org/news/podcasts/speaking-of-psychology/personality-tests.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [apa.org]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apa.org/about/policy/guidelines-psychological-assessment-evaluation.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [apa.org]}}\
Use the profile to choose behaviours to observe, not identities to adopt. Look for patterns across 
\f1\b specific incidents, trusted feedback, outcomes, and time
\f0\b0 . If the results are causing significant concern, or if the questionnaire was used for a consequential employment purpose, consider reviewing them confidentially with a qualified occupational psychologist who can examine the actual measure.\
Finally, do not use these labels to categorise colleagues, speculate about diagnoses, or share another person\'92s assessment without clear permission. Protect privacy, minimise unnecessary disclosure, and preserve everyone\'92s dignity, especially when power differences are involved.\
}